arter (next earnings disclosure)\",\n       \"value\": \"$109.02 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n       \"basis\": \"latest Zacks consensus estimate; +91.24% versus the year-ago quarter\",\n       \"party\": \"Zacks Investment Research (consensus estimate)\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"ev-2\",\n     \"summary\": \"Zacks Consensus Estimates project Nvidia's full-year earnings at $9.25 per share and revenue at $406.05 billion, representing increases of 93.92% and 88.04% respectively from the prior year.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"For the full year, the Zacks Consensus Estimates are projecting earnings of $9.25 per share and revenue of $406.05 billion, which would represent changes of +93.92% and +88.04%, respectively, from the prior year.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Zacks Investment Research (consensus estimate)\",\n     \"statement_date\": \"2026-09-28\",\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"Earnings per share\",\n       \"period\": \"full year\",\n       \"value\": \"$9.25\",\n       \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n       \"basis\": \"Zacks Consensus Estimate; +93.92% versus the prior year\",\n       \"party\": \"Zacks Investment Research (consensus estimate)\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 2,\n       \"measure\": \"Revenue\",\n       \"period\": \"full year\",\n       \"value\": \"$406.05 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n       \"basis\": \"Zacks Consensus Estimate; +88.04% versus the prior year\",\n       \"party\": \"Zacks Investment Research (consensus estimate)\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"ev-3\",\n     \"summary\": \"The Zacks Consensus EPS estimate for Nvidia shifted 4.73% upward over the past month, a revision Zacks says reflects analysts' more positive near-term view of the business.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"Over the past month, the Zacks Consensus EPS estimate has shifted 4.73% upward.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Zacks Investment Research\",\n     \"statement_date\": \"2026-09-28\",\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"Zacks Consensus EPS estimate revision\",\n       \"period\": \"past month\",\n       \"value\": \"4.73%\",\n       \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n       \"basis\": \"upward shift in the consensus EPS estimate over the past month\",\n       \"party\": \"Zacks Investment Research\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"answer\": \"B12\",\n   \"article\": 4,\n   \"statements_with_figures\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e1\",\n     \"summary\": \"Wall Street consensus, as reported by Motley Fool, expects Nvidia to grow revenue by 91% this year and 66% next year (the article later ties 'next year's earnings' to fiscal 2028, which ends in January 2028).\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"Wall Street expects the company to grow revenue by 91% this year and 66% next year.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Wall Street consensus\",\n     \"statement_date\": null,\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue growth\",\n       \"period\": \"this year\",\n       \"value\": \"91%\",\n       \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n       \"basis\": null,\n       \"party\": \"Wall Street consensus\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 2,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue growth\",\n       \"period\": \"next year\",\n       \"value\": \"66%\",\n       \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n       \"basis\": null,\n       \"party\": \"Wall Street consensus\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e2\",\n     \"summary\": \"Nvidia is expected by consensus to report earnings per share of $15.68 in fiscal 2028, which the article says ends in January 2028.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"For fiscal 2028, which ends in January of that year, Nvidia is expected to have earnings per share of $15.68.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Wall Street consensus\",\n     \"statement_date\": null,\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"earnings per share\",\n       \"period\": \"fiscal 2028, which ends in January of that year\",\n       \"value\": \"$15.68\",\n       \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n       \"basis\": null,\n       \"party\": \"Wall Street consensus\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"answer\": \"B18\",\n   \"article\": 5,\n   \"statements_with_figures\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e1\",\n     \"summary\": \"Nvidia reported revenue of $96.2 billion for its fiscal second quarter, 106% higher than the same period a year earlier, with a 75% gross margin.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"Nvidia ( NVDA +2.55% ) recently reported $96.2 billion in revenue for the fiscal second quarter, which was 106% more than in the same period last year. The company also produced a 75% gross margin\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Nvidia\",\n     \"statement_date\": null,\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue\",\n       \"period\": \"fiscal second quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"$96.2 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": \"company-wide\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 2,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue growth\",\n       \"period\": \"fiscal second quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"106%\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": \"year-over-year\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 3,\n       \"measure\": \"gross margin\",\n       \"period\": \"fiscal second quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"75%\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": \"company-wide\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e2\",\n     \"summary\": \"Nvidia guided to $108 billion in revenue for the current quarter, representing 17% sequential growth.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"Revenue and earnings both handily beat expectations, and Nvidia guided to a jaw-dropping $108 billion in revenue for the current quarter, representing 17% sequential growth.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Nvidia\",\n     \"statement_date\": null,\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue guidance\",\n       \"period\": \"current quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"$108 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n       \"basis\": \"company guidance\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 2,\n       \"measure\": \"sequential revenue growth\",\n       \"period\": \"current quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"17%\",\n       \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n       \"basis\": \"sequential, derived from company guidance\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e3\",\n     \"summary\": \"Nvidia management told investors to expect roughly 70% revenue growth in the next fiscal year.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"The company also produced a 75% gross margin, and management told investors to expect roughly 70% revenue growth in the next fiscal year.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Nvidia\",\n     \"statement_date\": null,\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue growth guidance\",\n       \"period\": \"next fiscal year\",\n       \"value\": \"roughly 70%\",\n       \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n       \"basis\": \"company guidance\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e4\",\n     \"summary\": \"Nvidia's total assets jumped by more than 50% over the past six months, with receivables rising from $38.5 billion in January to $63.1 billion at the end of July; the article calculates days sales outstanding rose from 45 to 60 days in one quarter.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"Nvidia's total assets jumped by more than 50% over the past six months.\",\n      \"A big part of that is the company's receivables rising from $38.5 billion in January to $63.1 billion at the end of July.\",\n      \"Nvidia's DSO went from 45 to 60 days in one quarter.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Nvidia\",\n     \"statement_date\": null,\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"total assets growth\",\n       \"period\": \"past six months\",\n       \"value\": \"more than 50%\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": \"company-wide\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 2,\n       \"measure\": \"receivables\",\n       \"period\": \"January\",\n       \"value\": \"$38.5 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": \"company-wide\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 3,\n       \"measure\": \"receivables\",\n       \"period\": \"end of July\",\n       \"value\": \"$63.1 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": \"company-wide\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 4,\n       \"measure\": \"days sales outstanding\",\n       \"period\": \"one quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"45 to 60 days\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": \"company-wide; calculated by article\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": [\n      {\n       \"question\": \"clean-1\",\n       \"new_question\": false,\n       \"reason\": \"Shows the balance-sheet scale of customer financing: receivables and days sales outstanding rose as Nvidia extended payment terms, informing the total credit-support question; these are not guarantee amounts.\"\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e6\",\n     \"summary\": \"Nvidia agreed to guarantee up to $105 billion of data center lease obligations for OpenAI.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"For example, Nvidia agreed to guarantee up to $105 billion of data center lease obligations for OpenAI.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Nvidia\",\n     \"statement_date\": null,\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"data center lease guarantee\",\n       \"period\": null,\n       \"value\": \"$105 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": \"up to; for OpenAI data center lease obligations\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": [\n      {\n       \"question\": \"clean-1\",\n       \"new_question\": false,\n       \"reason\": \"Directly informs the thesis's tracked amount of credit support and guarantees to AI labs/cloud partners: Nvidia agreed to guarantee up to $105 billion of OpenAI data center lease obligations.\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"answer\": \"B20\",\n   \"article\": 5,\n   \"statements_with_figures\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e1\",\n     \"summary\": \"Nvidia reported $96.2 billion of revenue for its fiscal second quarter, 106% more than in the same period a year earlier, at a 75% gross margin, according to the article's account of the company's recently reported quarter.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"Nvidia ( NVDA +2.55% ) recently reported $96.2 billion in revenue for the fiscal second quarter, which was 106% more than in the same period last year.\",\n      \"The company also produced a 75% gross margin\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Nvidia\",\n     \"statement_date\": \"recently\",\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue\",\n       \"period\": \"fiscal second quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"$96.2 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": \"company total revenue\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 2,\n       \"measure\": \"year-over-year revenue growth\",\n       \"period\": \"fiscal second quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"106%\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": \"versus same period last year\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 3,\n       \"measure\": \"gross margin\",\n       \"period\": \"fiscal second quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"75%\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": null,\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e2\",\n     \"summary\": \"Nvidia's management told investors to expect roughly 70% revenue growth in the next fiscal year, the article reports.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"The company also produced a 75% gross margin, and management told investors to expect roughly 70% revenue growth in the next fiscal year.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Nvidia\",\n     \"statement_date\": \"recently\",\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue growth\",\n       \"period\": \"next fiscal year\",\n       \"value\": \"roughly 70%\",\n       \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n       \"basis\": null,\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia management\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e3\",\n     \"summary\": \"Nvidia guided to a jaw-dropping $108 billion in revenue for its current quarter, which the article says represents 17% sequential growth.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"Revenue and earnings both handily beat expectations, and Nvidia guided to a jaw-dropping $108 billion in revenue for the current quarter, representing 17% sequential growth.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Nvidia\",\n     \"statement_date\": null,\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue\",\n       \"period\": \"current quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"$108 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n       \"basis\": null,\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia management\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 2,\n       \"measure\": \"sequential revenue growth\",\n       \"period\": \"current quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"17%\",\n       \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n       \"basis\": \"sequential, versus the reported fiscal second quarter\",\n       \"party\": \"fool.com (article author's calculation from the guidance)\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e4\",\n     \"summary\": \"Nvidia's total assets jumped by more than 50% over the past six months, driven in large part by receivables rising from $38.5 billion in January to $63.1 billion at the end of July; the article calculates that days sales outstanding rose from 45 to 60 days in one quarter, meaning customers are taking longer to pay.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"However, a closer look at the company's balance sheet shows that Nvidia's total assets jumped by more than 50% over the past six months.\",\n      \"As mentioned earlier, Nvidia's total assets grew rapidly. A big part of that is the company's receivables rising from $38.5 billion in January to $63.1 billion at the end of July.\",\n      \"Nvidia's DSO went from 45 to 60 days in one quarter. Customers are taking longer to pay.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Nvidia\",\n     \"statement_date\": null,\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"total assets growth\",\n       \"period\": \"over the past six months\",\n       \"value\": \"more than 50%\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": \"company balance sheet\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 2,\n       \"measure\": \"receivables\",\n       \"period\": \"January\",\n       \"value\": \"$38.5 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": null,\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 3,\n       \"measure\": \"receivables\",\n       \"period\": \"end of July\",\n       \"value\": \"$63.1 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": null,\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 4,\n       \"measure\": \"days sales outstanding (DSO)\",\n       \"period\": \"one quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"45 to 60 days\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": \"average collection period calculated from reported figures\",\n       \"party\": \"fool.com (article author's calculation)\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": [\n      {\n       \"question\": \"clean-1\",\n       \"new_question\": false,\n       \"reason\": \"Receivables growth and the rise in days sales outstanding are the working-capital counterpart of Nvidia helping finance customers' orders; the article links part of it to extended payment terms (separate item). It is not itself a guarantee or a credit-support commitment counted toward the thesis's disclosed-amount outcome, but it informs how the support is showing up on the balance sheet.\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"answer\": \"B22\",\n   \"article\": 5,\n   \"statements_with_figures\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e1\",\n     \"summary\": \"Nvidia reported $96.2 billion of revenue for its fiscal second quarter, 106% more than in the same period a year earlier, at a 75% gross margin; the article says revenue and earnings handily beat expectations.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"Nvidia ( NVDA +2.55% ) recently reported $96.2 billion in revenue for the fiscal second quarter, which was 106% more than in the same period last year. The company also produced a 75% gross margin\",\n      \"Revenue and earnings both handily beat expectations\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Nvidia\",\n     \"statement_date\": null,\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue\",\n       \"period\": \"fiscal second quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"$96.2 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": null,\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 2,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue growth\",\n       \"period\": \"fiscal second quarter versus same period last year\",\n       \"value\": \"106%\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": \"growth over the same period last year\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 3,\n       \"measure\": \"gross margin\",\n       \"period\": \"fiscal second quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"75%\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": null,\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e2\",\n     \"summary\": \"Nvidia guided investors to $108 billion of revenue for the current quarter, which it said represents 17% sequential growth.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"Nvidia guided to a jaw-dropping $108 billion in revenue for the current quarter, representing 17% sequential growth.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Nvidia\",\n     \"statement_date\": null,\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue guidance\",\n       \"period\": \"current quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"$108 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n       \"basis\": null,\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 2,\n       \"measure\": \"sequential revenue growth\",\n       \"period\": \"current quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"17%\",\n       \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n       \"basis\": \"sequential growth\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e3\",\n     \"summary\": \"Nvidia management told investors to expect roughly 70% revenue growth in the next fiscal year.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"management told investors to expect roughly 70% revenue growth in the next fiscal year.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Nvidia\",\n     \"statement_date\": null,\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue growth guidance\",\n       \"period\": \"next fiscal year\",\n       \"value\": \"70%\",\n       \"kind\": \"guidance\",\n       \"basis\": \"roughly\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"e5\",\n     \"summary\": \"Nvidia's receivables rose from $38.5 billion in January to $63.1 billion at the end of July, as total assets jumped by more than 50% over the past six months, and days sales outstanding rose from 45 to 60 days in one quarter; Nvidia said it extended payment terms on large orders from certain customers.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"A big part of that is the company's receivables rising from $38.5 billion in January to $63.1 billion at the end of July.\",\n      \"Nvidia's DSO went from 45 to 60 days in one quarter. Customers are taking longer to pay.\",\n      \"To be fair, Nvidia told us why. The company extended payment terms on large orders from certain customers.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"Nvidia\",\n     \"statement_date\": null,\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"accounts receivable\",\n       \"period\": \"January\",\n       \"value\": \"$38.5 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": null,\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 2,\n       \"measure\": \"accounts receivable\",\n       \"period\": \"end of July\",\n       \"value\": \"$63.1 billion\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": null,\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 3,\n       \"measure\": \"days sales outstanding\",\n       \"period\": \"one quarter\",\n       \"value\": \"60 days\",\n       \"kind\": \"actual\",\n       \"basis\": \"up from 45 days\",\n       \"party\": \"Nvidia\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": [\n      {\n       \"question\": \"clean-1\",\n       \"new_question\": false,\n       \"reason\": \"Shows NVIDIA financing customers' purchases through extended payment terms on large orders, alongside the formal guarantees the thesis tracks; the receivables jump and DSO rise of 45 to 60 days indicate the scale of that customer credit exposure, but the item gives no guarantee amounts.\"\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"answer\": \"B23\",\n   \"article\": 4,\n   \"statements_with_figures\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"ev-1\",\n     \"summary\": \"Motley Fool contributor Jeremy Bowman reported that Wall Street expects Nvidia to grow revenue by 91% this year and 66% next year, and that Nvidia is expected to earn $15.68 per share in fiscal 2028, which the article says ends in January of that year. These are third-party/consensus forecasts, not company guidance; the article gives no period year for the two revenue growth rates beyond 'this year' and 'next year'.\",\n     \"passages\": [\n      \"Wall Street expects the company to grow revenue by 91% this year and 66% next year. For fiscal 2028, which ends in January of that year, Nvidia is expected to have earnings per share of $15.68.\"\n     ],\n     \"statement_party\": \"consensus\",\n     \"statement_date\": null,\n     \"figures\": [\n      {\n       \"n\": 1,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue growth\",\n       \"period\": \"this year\",\n       \"value\": \"91%\",\n       \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n       \"basis\": \"company revenue growth, attributed to Wall Street expectations\",\n       \"party\": \"consensus\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 2,\n       \"measure\": \"revenue growth\",\n       \"period\": \"next year\",\n       \"value\": \"66%\",\n       \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n       \"basis\": \"company revenue growth, attributed to Wall Street expectations\",\n       \"party\": \"consensus\"\n      },\n      {\n       \"n\": 3,\n       \"measure\": \"earnings per share\",\n       \"period\": \"fiscal 2028, which ends in January of that year\",\n       \"value\": \"$15.68\",\n       \"kind\": \"estimate\",\n       \"basis\": \"expected EPS, source not named beyond 'expected'\",\n       \"party\": \"consensus\"\n      }\n     ],\n     \"links\": \"none\"\n    }\n   ]\n  }\n ]\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; d=json.load(open(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/figure-fields-2/settle-packet-part1.json\\\")); [(print(\\\"ARTICLE\\\",a[\\\"article\\\"],a[\\\"title\\\"],a[\\\"publication_date\\\"],\\\"\\\\n\\\",a[\\\"text\\\"],\\\"\\\\nNAMED\\\",a.get(\\\"named_figures\\\"))) for a in d[\\\"articles\\\"] if a[\\\"article\\\"] not in (4,5,9)]'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; d=json.load(open(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/figure-fields-2/settle-packet-part1.json\\\")); [(print(\\\"ARTICLE\\\",a[\\\"article\\\"],a[\\\"title\\\"],a[\\\"publication_date\\\"],\\\"\\\\n\\\",a[\\\"text\\\"],\\\"\\\\nNAMED\\\",a.get(\\\"named_figures\\\"))) for a in d[\\\"articles\\\"] if a[\\\"article\\\"] not in (4,5,9)]'\"","aggregated_output":"ARTICLE 10 When Should You Buy NVIDIA Stock After This Run? 2026-09-28 \n When Should You Buy NVIDIA Stock After This Run?\nA $10,000 holding in NVIDIA (NVDA) stock three months ago was worth about $11,700 as of September 25, 2026. Yet against profits, the shares still trade near the low end of their ten-year range. If you have been waiting to buy NVIDIA, have you already missed it?\nHave You Missed The Low Multiple On NVIDIA Stock?\nNot if you judge it by earnings against its own past. The price-to-earnings ratio, or P/E, is the share price divided by a year of profit per share. NVIDIA trades at 28.1 times earnings , above the 22.1 for the S&P 500. Over the past ten years its P/E has ranged from 19.6 to 143.1, and today it is near the bottom.\nBut a low P/E only stays low if profit holds up. NVIDIA’s operating margin, the share of revenue left after running costs, is 65%, its highest in ten years. Its three-year average is 59%. If margins slipped back toward that average, the same price would buy less profit.\nCash looks less comfortable than earnings. Against operating cash flow, the cash the business brings in from running itself, the stock costs 40.4 times. The S&P 500 costs 14.5 times. Part of the cash has gone into inventory. On the fiscal Q2 2027 call, management said inventory rose to $32 billion as NVIDIA prepared for the Vera Rubin launch. On earnings or on cash, a price built on peak margins needs profit growth to continue.\nHow Much Revenue Is NVIDIA Stock Counting On?\nThe price appears to assume more revenue than NVIDIA itself has forecast for fiscal Q3 2027. Management guided revenue for that quarter to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%. The consensus forecast for that quarter is $111.3 billion, above the top of that range.\nThat expectation has a record behind it. Management said fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of $96 billion more than doubled from a year earlier. Growth also sped up for the fourth quarter in a row.\nThe newly launched Vera Rubin platform is one source of that revenue. Management expects it to make up about 20% of data center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027. Management says supply, not demand, is the limit. Management expects supply to remain a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028.\nGross margin, the share of revenue left after making the product, is a different measure from operating margin. For fiscal Q3 2027 it is guided to 74%, plus or minus half a point, down from 75% in fiscal Q2 2027. Management pointed to higher component costs, especially memory. The next report has to beat NVIDIA’s own revenue forecast. The stock has not always taken its reports well.\nNVIDIA’s Fiscal Q3 2027 Results Land in November\nNVIDIA is expected to report on or around November 17, 2026. That report covers fiscal Q3 2027, and it will show whether revenue matches what the price appears to assume.\nThe stock’s record after reports runs both ways. Over the last six reports, NVIDIA shares fell after four and rose after two, measured over two trading days. The biggest drop was 9.4%, after the February 25, 2026, report. The biggest gain was 3.8%, after the August 26, 2026, report.\nA broad market sell-off is a separate risk. During the 2025 tariff shock, NVIDIA stock fell 32% from peak to low, against 19% for the S&P 500.\nIf fiscal Q3 2027 revenue lands below $111.3 billion, the price will have asked for more than NVIDIA delivered. Buying now would then prove early. Suppose revenue clears $111.3 billion and gross margin comes in at 74% or better. The business will then have kept pace with the run. Buying at today’s price would not have been too late. \nNAMED [{'figure': 1, 'text': 'the $111.3 billion consensus forecast for the quarter'}, {'figure': 2, 'text': 'the $108 billion revenue guided for the quarter'}]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; d=json.load(open(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/figure-fields-2/settle-packet-part1.json\\\"));\nfor a in d[\\\"answers\\\"]:\n print(\\\"ANSWER\\\",a[\\\"answer\\\"],\\\"ARTICLE\\\",a[\\\"article\\\"])\n for s in a[\\\"statements_with_figures\\\"]:\n  print(\\\"STAT\\\",s[\\\"id\\\"],\\\"party\\\",s.get(\\\"statement_party\\\"),\\\"date\\\",s.get(\\\"statement_date\\\"),\\\"summary\\\",s[\\\"summary\\\"],\\\"links\\\",s.get(\\\"links\\\",\\\"ABSENT\\\"))\n  for f in s[\\\"figures\\\"]: print(\\\"FIG\\\",f[\\\"n\\\"],f[\\\"measure\\\"],f[\\\"value\\\"],f[\\\"kind\\\"],\\\"party\\\",f[\\\"party\\\"],\\\"basis\\\",f.get(\\\"basis\\\"))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
